WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:03.940
OT detection begins with an accurate understanding of the environment.

2
00:00:04.040 --> 00:00:13.320
Asset inventory should identify systems, owners, locations, functions, criticality, software or firmware where known, and expected communication.

3
00:00:13.420 --> 00:00:18.060
An address without operational identity is weak detection context.

4
00:00:18.340 --> 00:00:27.140
A Purdue-style view can organize field, control, supervisory, site-operations, industrial-DMZ, and enterprise functions.

5
00:00:27.240 --> 00:00:31.160
The model is a reference, not a substitute for the real architecture.

6
00:00:31.260 --> 00:00:39.420
Document zones, conduits, serial and wireless paths, vendor connections, and services that cross boundaries.

7
00:00:39.700 --> 00:00:43.380
PLCs and RTUs execute or support control.

8
00:00:43.480 --> 00:00:49.960
HMIs and SCADA platforms give operators process visibility and supervisory authority.

9
00:00:50.060 --> 00:00:52.780
Historians preserve process data.

10
00:00:52.880 --> 00:00:56.080
Engineering workstations contain privileged programming tools.

11
00:00:56.180 --> 00:01:00.020
Remote-access systems connect support personnel to selected assets.

12
00:01:00.120 --> 00:01:04.440
Each role produces different evidence and different consequences.

13
00:01:04.720 --> 00:01:09.440
Map detection use cases to critical assets and communication paths.

14
00:01:09.540 --> 00:01:18.180
An unexpected peer is more meaningful when the detection knows it contacted a controller, crossed an industrial DMZ, or used an engineering pathway.

15
00:01:18.280 --> 00:01:23.160
Asset function and process ownership also determine who should validate the alert.

16
00:01:23.440 --> 00:01:26.800
Architecture reveals dependencies and blind spots.

17
00:01:26.900 --> 00:01:35.220
A sensor may not be visible on IP networks, a gateway may hide serial devices, and a central historian may represent many sites.

18
00:01:35.320 --> 00:01:39.720
A detection that assumes complete network visibility can produce false confidence.

19
00:01:40.000 --> 00:01:43.760
Keep context current through change control and collaboration.

20
00:01:43.860 --> 00:01:52.340
Operations and engineering teams can explain maintenance patterns, redundancy, control modes, and safe escalation.

21
00:01:52.440 --> 00:02:01.320
Detection engineers translate that knowledge into asset enrichment, expected behavior, and response guidance that analysts can use under pressure.
